  Scenario: Positive: create Resource Type with tags
    Given Resource Admin wants to create a new Resource Type with the following attributes
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-3",
         "name": "FAQ-3",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag3",
            "tag4"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin creates a new Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type is created successfully with response code 201
    And return the created resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-3",
         "name": "FAQ-3",
         "description": "  ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag3",
            "tag4"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: create Resource Type with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given an existing Resource Type from the project A with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' as the following attributes
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-4",
         "name": "FAQ-4",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    And the Resource Admin from the project B with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' wants to Create a new Resource Type with the same Key
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-4",
         "name": "FAQ-4",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin creates a new Resource Type with an existing or duplicate key
    Then the Resource Type is created successfully with response code 201
    And return the created resource type
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ-4",
         "name": "FAQ-4",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """

  Scenario: Negative: create Resource Type with key: empty
    Given Resource Admin wants to create a new Resource Type with an empty key
      """json
      {
         "key": "",
         "name": "FAQ-4",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ]
      }
      """
    When the Resource Admin creates a new Resource Type
    Then the Resource Type creation fails with response code 400
    And the response body includes status 400 and error message 'Bad Request'

  Scenario: Negative: create Resource Type with key: null
    Given Resource Admin wants to create a new Resource Type with a null key
      """json
